{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:cb23a564558d8909","name":"Mercenary Soldier","source":{"id":"source:reference-cb23a564558d8909","title":"Mercenary Soldier","revision":18976,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:04:28Z","sha256":"b8d46b9d82b5efeda1088a610d4359ad510fdfcb4129720c9e2f18548e1927e4","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18976","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Mercenary%20Soldier&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-cb23a564558d8909","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Mercenaries are professional soldiers who fight for anyone who will pay them. Their loyalty extends only so long as the credits keep rolling in, and even then they might break a contract if the job sours or seems hopeless. A mercenary doesn't sign on for causes and doesn't care about the nature or identity of their employer, only that they are paid and paid on time. Their fickle nature and lack of regard for the reasons behind a conflict make mercenaries unattractive soldiers for many, but for those who have coin to spend and are desperate enough, a company of mercenaries can make do in the absence of more disciplined troops.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mercenaries"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mercenaries","referenceId":"reference:7db5f4a3b7fe5a00"}," are organized in the same ways as other military units. Mercenary Soldiers make up the bulk of the fighting unit, and supporting them are numerous ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mercenary Scouts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mercenary_Scouts"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mercenary Heavy Infantry"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mercenary_Heavy_Infantry","referenceId":"reference:f4ced2e61ef43eb7"},".\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Mercenary Soldier Statistics (